      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The 1969 Hurricane Camille caused flash flooding, reversing James River flow for three miles and damaging Norwood.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/norwood_nelson_county_virginia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Cabell family’s 1738 land patent of 4,800 acres founded plantations like Soldier’s Joy (built 1785) and Montezuma.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
